WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:05.400
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.634
Hey, before we get started,
everyone do me a favor.

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.534
Check under your seats for
any classified documents from

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:10.634
The White House.

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:15.567
They just seem to be
everywhere lately.

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:17.033
Yeah, everyone is
talking about this.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:19.367
A second batch
of classified documents

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.300
were found at President Biden's
home in Delaware.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.968
Good Lord. Apparently,
presidents lose

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.133
classified documents
the way we lose AirPods.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.934
It's like...

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.000
It's getting crazy.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.367
Now, instead of quarters,

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.601
Biden's finding classified
documents behind kids' ears.

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.267
It's like, "Oh, look at that.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:38.567
The nuclear codes from Iran."

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:42.267
Yeah, most of the new documents
were found in Biden's garage.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.801
Come on. These are the nation's
top secrets.

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.868
They should all be stored in
that crazy puzzle box from

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:49.167
"Knives Out 2."

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.234
"Aim it towards..."

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:53.367
Another classified document
was found in a room

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:56.100
that Biden calls
his personal library.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.634
Oh, please. Just say bathroom.

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.501
You know? I mean...

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.434
The White House said it was just

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:05.601
a small number of
classified documents.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:06.767
That's like your doctor saying,
"Don't worry.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.901
It's just a smidge of herpes."

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:19.734
"Barely -- barely...

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:23.634
Just an unch, just an unch."

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.634
This morning,
Biden addressed the discovery

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:26.934
of the second batch
of documents,

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:28.033
and here's what he said.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:30.868
-People know I
take classified documents

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.534
and classified materials
seriously.

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:34.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.801
-Here's how Fox News aired it.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.701
-People know I take
classified documents.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.434
♪♪
-There you go.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:51.467
Interesting.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.767
But the Justice Department is
taking this seriously.

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:56.634
Today, the attorney general
appointed a special counsel

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:59.167
to investigate Biden's
handling of the documents.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:01.334
Yeah. I'm not saying
Biden's getting worried,

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.200
but he just texted
Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.367
So, you go, "Wow!
That's not good.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.133
That's not good."

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:09.667
That's right -- they appointed
a special counsel.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:10.834
Biden tried to spin it.

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:14.167
He said, "Good news --
I'm creating jobs."

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.734
But The White House
is now saying that

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:17.300
they are confident
an investigation will show

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.334
the documents were
inadvertently misplaced.

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:21.567
Next, he'll be like,

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:25.133
"I was just holding it for
a friend, I swear."

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:28.033
Switching gears, I saw that
Prince Harry's memoir, "Spare,"

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:29.634
is breaking sales records.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:30.767
It is massive.

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:31.901
And this is very interesting --

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:34.267
his book deal
includes three more books.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:36.267
So he's already working
on sequels.

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:37.400
In fact, we got our hands on

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.334
some of the titles
that he's considering.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:41.300
-Oh, here we go.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.234
-What's up, Tariq?

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:44.300
-Let me guess.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.968
You're going to poke fun
at Prince Harry

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:48.467
by listing a bunch of
fake book titles.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.767
-I mean, yeah,
that was the plan.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.534
-I know exactly
how this will go down.

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:55.567
So, you'll show a graphic
with a picture of Prince Harry

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.767
that says, "New Book Titles."

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:01.901
And then, under that, you'll
list a bunch of jokes like...

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.567
Or...

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.667
-Yeah, yeah, maybe.
-Or...

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.734
And then you'll do...

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.901
-Yeah.
-Or...

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.467
-Uh-huh.
-And then...

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.667
-Yeah.
-Or...

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:28.667
-That's right.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.467
-Then, finally,
you'll just do...

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:32.601
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.667
-Is that how
it's going to go, Jimmy?

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.267
-Uh, yeah, you nailed it.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.100
-It's a fun bit.
You should do it on the show.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.567
-Well, maybe some other time.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:47.000
Got some TV news.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.200
"Wheel of Fortune" was just
renewed for five more seasons,

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.400
and the deal includes
a big raise for Pat Sajak.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.534
You can tell Pat's excited.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.133
Check out
one of today's puzzles.

00:03:57.701 --> 00:04:00.367
-I'll take a "C."

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:01.901
-Yeah, that's it.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.868
-Come on! What --
-Wow! Don't rub it in.

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:11.334
-Did you guys see this?

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:15.200
I heard that Subway might be
sold for more than $10 billion.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.200
Yeah, the sale could be done
in a few months

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.267
or a little longer if they want
their Subway toasted.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:27.767
And, finally, after being closed
for years due to COVID,

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.267
the public bathrooms in several

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:32.267
New York City subway
stations were just reopened.

00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:34.901
-Whoo-hoo!
-Yeah.

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:36.334
And you're not going to
believe this.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.167
When they opened them up, they
found more classified documents.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:39.300
-What?!

